  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 259 AM CDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\nThe LREF is continuing to show a large ridge building over the \ncentral CONUS over the weekend with northwest flow setting up over \nMissouri and Illinois.  Less than 15-20% of NBM/LREF members are \nproducing any rain over the area from Saturday night through next \nThursday favoring mainly a dry forecast.  It does look to be hot and \nhumid as 850mb temperatures increase into the 22-26C range (>95th \npercentile) supporting highs in the 90s.  The warmest day at this \npoint looks to be Monday as the NBM IQR at St. Louis is only 3 \ndegrees with highs in the mid to upper 90s.  With dewpoints forecast \nto be in the 60s and 70s, afternoon heat indexes on Sunday into \nTuesday will likely climb above 100 degrees in most areas with some \nareas reaching above 105.   There is some indication as the pattern \ncontinues to amplify by the middle of next week, a weak front will \nmove in from the east which will cause a slight drop in temperatures \nproviding some relief.",
